                *****************************************
                *                                       *
                *    C a r d G u p p i e s - I I I      *
                *                                       *
                *          A Xenolink doorgame          *
                *                                       *
                *****************************************




This will be the last version ever to be published of the famous CardGuppies
doorgame range. This version replaces _all_ earlier versions ever released.

CardGuppies-II enhancements, support or bug fixes are out of the question.

This version is no longer freeware. If you want to use this game, you have
to pay your shareware fee (10$).



                             Introduction
                             ------------

Why a new version ? Well, like most doorgames, if you didn't play the game
every day, the chance on winning was practical speaking "nil".

To overcome this problem, a config file is now supported by CardGuppies-III.
In this config file, the Sysop is able to "tune" the game. He can specify
the maximum number of plays per month allowed.

By default, a player may only play 25 times a month, giving "all day callers"
no major benefit to them who can not play every day. This parameter can be
set to a value between 15 and 31. Specifying 31 will practically speaking
turn CardGuppies-III into CardGuppies-II again.

Well, there was a config file now, so an user asked feature has also been
accomplished. The Sysop can now specify wether he want the user's real name
or his alias name to be used in the game.


                            The game
                            --------

A helpfile with "how to play" is provided, and can be read by entering a
questionmark (?) during the game.

Playing the game is rather simple. First, some general information will be
shown on your screen. Here you will be told about the current leader of the
game, and your financial position so far. Then, you will enter the game.

The playfield consist of 3 rows with playing cards. The goal is to guess the
value of the next face down card. This is done by simply saying H(igher) or
L(ower). Then you will be asked to place your bet. If your bet is correct,
the money will be added to your account, otherwise, you loose the money.

If the next card has the same value, then the higher/lower status will be
determined by the card colours. Spades is the highest, followed by Hearts,
Diamonds and Clubs. So, the card's suit take *ONLY* precedence when the
cards match in value.

Per row, you can (only) once change the current card for the face down card
on the left. You may do this if the current card is not so good to bet on.
At the end of each row, the last card shown will be transported to the next
row. On the last row, you must bet at least the half of your money.

Each of the 52 playing cards are represented only once. This means, that you
can never get the same card twice. Furthermore, only one joker can be drawn.
In this case, you must guess the value of the next card. If wrong, nothing
happens to your money. If guessed right, then one million $ plus the amount
of money of the current leader of the game will be added to your account.

Every 10 million $ you've earned will be replaced by a "bank".

Your earnings for the day will be shown if you're ready with the game. Your
score will then be awarded against the other users playing, and a highscore
will be calculated and shown.


                        Setting up the game
                        -------------------

In order to make CardGuppies-III work on your BBS system, you have to take
the following actions :

1. Create a directory, called DOORS:CardGuppies-III
2. Copy all files of the package to this directory.
3. Edit the configuration file to your desires.
4. Edit your doorgames menu so that you can play the game.
   This is NOT a multi-user doorgame !!!.
    
   Example:
   
      CMD = "C"
        {
           XenolinkDoor "CardGuppies-III/CardGuppies-III"
        }   


The first time CardGuppies-III is run, two files will be created :
- DOORS:CardGuppies-III/Month      ; Registrates the current month playing in
- DOORS:CardGuppies-III/Players    ; Current players for this month
Highscores will be placed in XBULLETINS:, called CG3.High.


After one month of playing, the game will automaticly start all over again,
whenever a player starts the game. The old players file will be renamed to
DOORS:CardGuppies-III/LastMonthPlayers. The old highscore file will be
renamed to XBULLETINS:CG3_LastMonth.High. You can use these files whenever a
calamity has happened with CardGuppies-III (e.g. an illegal restart due to
bugs, crashes or so ...), or for granting some privileges to the last month
top CardGuppies-III player.


                               CG3 Editor
                               ----------

Calling DOORS:CardGuppies-III/CG3_Editor (CLI program!) will open the player
file, and enables you (as mighty Sysop) to change some fields in the player
file. The program is very simple, so no manual about how to operate is
needed. One point, however, make sure nobody is playing the game while you're
using the CG3_Editor. I haven't used any locking whatsoever, simply because
you basicly never need this editor.

The CG3_Editor is also being used to enter a registration key. It will
perform one dimensional checking on the given input. However, CardGuppies
uses a two dimensional encryption mechanism.



                              Registration
                              ------------

CardGuppies-II was released as postcard ware. Seeing the _mighty_ response
to this low-cost system (7 cards ...), and given the fact that on almost any
Xenolink BBS I've ever logged on, CardGuppies-II was installed, this version
will NO LONGER be low-cost postcard ware. Postcards reaching me after the
9th of november 1992 will no longer be accepted as a sign of "good will".

I'm NOT very font about registration, shareware fees and so on, but it seems
to be very hard to do such a little job of sending one simple postcard
(costs about 2 $ ...). If this is the general way of Amiga fans to show
their gratitude to those who have spent many many hours to create doorgames,
then I'm very disappointed by this way of behaviour.

You can run CardGuppies-III without a registration key, BUT:
- Users get an explicit warning that you've installed a non registrated
  CardGuppies-III version.
- No highscore file will be created.
- Each player's highscore will be set on 0 banks, 20$ afterwards.


If you want to registrate your version :

Send me 10$, the exact name you want to register under, and the exact name
you want your BBS system to be announced on the display. Both names may not
exceed the resp. 23 and 24 characters. An example :

               Name : [Wim Rumping]            (11 chars, max = 23 chars)
               BBS  : [BBS Het Enge Bos]       (16 chars, max = 24 chars)


Send all this to the following address :

               Name     : J. Bleumink
               Address  : Zamenhof 6
               City+Zip : 1961 GL Heemskerk
               Country  : The Netherlands

You will then receive a letter with your registration key on paper. This key
can be entered with the CG3_Editor provided. The key consist of 10 lines
with 12 hex characters on each line. If entered succesful, you can then
enjoy the FULL functionallity of the game.

Dutch BBS systems can registrate for hfl. 15,- (app. 9.4 $). Just drop me a
mail, and I will upload a key file onto your BBS.

The registration will take place on personal title, so they can not be sold
to another person !!! (Why should you, the price is low enough ...) The key
file is like a credit card, only you are authorized to use it.

The registration key can be entered using the CG3_Editor program.
You can also enter your registration key directly into a key.file. To do
this, you should create the file DOORS:CardGuppies-III/key.file. Then you
can enter the 10 datalines directly. Be sure that each line consist out of
12 characters, with no leading spaces, tabs or what-so-ever. No spaces may
be entered between the characters, e.g.:

012345678901   (line 1)
012345678901
   .
   .
012345678901   (line 10)

The preferred way is to enter your key.file with the CG3_Editor.


What happens with your money ??? It will not disapear into the big hole of
my wallet. I'll use some of it to send the registration card back to you.
The rest of the money will be used as "savings" for new development tools
for my Amiga. It will also be used for supporting the development of
Xenolink doorgames (to pay my bill to call to the new testsite :-) ).



