                       Internal error messages
                       -----------------------

The following list of messages can be 'presented' to the user :

o Call your sysop ... Amiga's internal time is corrupt
- Reading Amiga's internal time returned an invalid time/date. Resetting
  your Amiga should correct this invalid time/date.

o Call your sysop ... The month file is corrupt
- How can this happen ? Well, using version 2.1 up should prevent this ...
  You can fix this by running CG3_Editor.

o Call your sysop ... could not create new month file
- Probably out of disk space ...

o Call your sysop ... he's out of memory (1)...
- The very first memory allocation failed ... CardGuppies-III will exit.
  No memory lost however ...
  
o Call your sysop ... he's out of memory (2)...
  Some previous allocated memory has been lost ...
- While creating an internal memory list for all players, you ran out of
  memory. Sorry, this version does not contain a 'memory fixer', so the
  only way to get out of this, is restarting your Amiga. Don't panic, in
  normal cases, all allocated memory will be freed up. CG3 does not need
  much memory at all ...

o Call your sysop ... could not create player file
- Probably out of disk space ...

o Fatal internal error ... contact your sysop ...
  Entry = ***GGGG***        
  Tell this  ^^^^ to your sysop ...
- How can this happen? This can't happen! But if it does, please send me
  the HEX code displayed between the stars!

o Call your sysop ... could not create highscore file
- Probably out of disk space ...

o You're key.file is not correct
  Each data line should contain at least 12 characters
  Delete old key.file, and reenter your key data
- Lines in key.file are not long enough.

o You're key.file is not correct
  A checksum error has been detected on line DD
  Delete old key.file, and reenter your key data
- If you use CG3_Editor for entering your key.file, then this error will
  not occur.

o Early EOF detected for key.file
  Delete old key.file, and reenter your key data
- Your key.file should contain at least 10 datalines.



